
 1   WHO IS RESPONSIBLE FOR YOUR DATA

PlexTickets is a self-hosted support ticket bot. It is operated by JMA Group ("we", "us"), the team running the JMA Group Discord server. We decide why and how the data described below is processed, which makes us the data controller under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

The bot runs on our own virtual machine, located in Germany. It is not a public or commercial service: it is used exclusively inside the JMA Group Discord server, and only members of that server can interact with it.

Contact for privacy matters: support.jma@proton.me

  2  WHAT DATA WE PROCESS

When you open a ticket or take part in one, the bot processes:

    Discord identifiers — your Discord user ID (a numeric identifier) and your Discord username / display name;
    Luanti username — the in-game username you give us (Luanti, formerly Minetest);
    Ticket content — every message you send inside the ticket, including text, links, and any screenshots, files or logs you attach;
    Other information you volunteer — anything else you choose to include in a ticket, for example descriptions of an issue or excerpts of server logs;
    Ticket metadata — ticket number, category, opening and closing timestamps, which staff member claimed or handled the ticket, and its status.

We do not collect your e-mail address, IP address, payment details, or any special categories of personal data (such as health, religious or political information), and we do not ask for them. The bot only processes messages in the channels it is configured for — the ticket panel and the ticket channels themselves — and not messages elsewhere on the server.

Because the bot runs inside Discord, Discord Inc. also processes your data as the platform provider, independently of us, under Discord's own Privacy Policy (https://discord.com/privacy).

  3  BOT DIRECT MESSAGES (DMs)

The Bot may send you direct messages (DMs) in the following situations:

    When you create a ticket — to confirm receipt and provide a ticket number
    When your ticket is closed — to notify you and optionally provide a transcript

These DMs are automated notifications related to ticket handling. They contain no data beyond the notification itself.

You can stop receiving these DMs by:

    Blocking the Bot on Discord (you will lose access to ticket notifications)
    Muting the Bot's messages using Discord's built-in options
    Disabling direct messages from server members in your Discord settings (may also affect ticket notifications)

If you block the Bot, we may not be able to notify you about your ticket status.

  4  WHY WE PROCESS IT, AND ON WHAT LEGAL BASIS

We use your data only to:

    handle your request and provide support — legal basis: our legitimate interest in operating our community and helping members (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), and/or performance of a service you use (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR);
    keep a record of past tickets, so we can follow up, avoid duplicate work and stay consistent — legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f));
    enforce server rules and investigate abuse or fraud — legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f));
    process extra information you volunteer (logs, screenshots, etc.) — your consent, given by submitting it (Art. 6(1)(a)). You can withdraw that consent at any time by asking us to delete it.

We do not use your data for advertising, profiling, or any purpose unrelated to support.

 5   THIRD-PARTY AI SERVICE FOR FAQ MATCHING

When you submit a ticket, your initial message may be automatically checked against our FAQ using DeepSeek, an artificial intelligence service provided by Hangzhou DeepSeek Artificial Intelligence Co., Ltd. (China).

What happens:

    The text of your ticket opening message is sent to DeepSeek's API
    DeepSeek analyzes the message and returns potential FAQ matches
    Based on the match confidence, the bot provides an automated first response
    You can then decide whether the FAQ answer resolves your issue or choose to continue to human staff

What this means for your data:

    Your message text is processed by DeepSeek's servers in China
    DeepSeek may retain this data according to its own privacy policy (https://cdn.deepseek.com/policies/en-US/deepseek-privacy-policy.html)
    This involves international data transfer outside the EU/EEA to a country without an adequacy decision

You can bypass this step:

    If you do not want your message processed by DeepSeek, simply ignore the automated FAQ response and continue communicating directly with staff. No further automated processing occurs after the initial check.

Legal basis:

    We rely on our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR) in improving support efficiency by providing quick automated answers when your question matches known FAQs.

   6 WHO CAN SEE YOUR DATA

Access is limited to JMA Group server staff holding the staff role(s) that grant visibility of ticket channels and the bot's logs. Individual tickets are visible to the ticket creator and to staff.

We do not sell, rent or share your data with third parties. We disclose data only:

    to staff members who need it to handle your ticket;
    to DeepSeek for the limited purpose of FAQ matching (see section 5);
    if we are legally obliged to, for example in response to a valid request from law enforcement or a court;
    where necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.

Service providers involved: Discord Inc. (the platform the bot runs on), DeepSeek (FAQ matching service), and our hosting infrastructure (our own VM in Germany). Our own storage stays in Germany. Where providers such as Discord or DeepSeek process data outside the EU/EEA, that happens under their own transfer mechanisms.

 7   HOW LONG WE KEEP IT

    Open tickets: for as long as the ticket is active.
    Closed tickets and their transcripts: 12 months after closure, then deleted automatically.
    Backups: copies are retained for 30 days, then overwritten.
    Exceptions: we may keep individual tickets longer if they are part of an ongoing investigation, a ban or appeal record, or if we are legally required to.

Note: We have no control over how long DeepSeek retains your data. Please refer to DeepSeek's own privacy policy for their retention practices (https://cdn.deepseek.com/policies/en-US/deepseek-privacy-policy.html).

 8   HOW WE PROTECT YOUR DATA

    Ticket channels are restricted to the ticket creator and staff roles.
    Access to the bot's database and logs requires a staff account, and is limited to the staff who need it.
    The VM is reachable only via SSH keys / VPN, with two-factor authentication on administrative accounts.
    Data is transmitted over encrypted connections (HTTPS/TLS) to all third-party services.
    Old tickets are deleted according to the schedule in section 7.

No system can be guaranteed completely secure, but we take these measures to keep the risk low.

 9   YOUR RIGHTS

Under the GDPR you have the right to:

    access the personal data we hold about you;
    correct inaccurate data;
    delete your data (right to be forgotten);
    restrict how we process it;
    object to processing based on our legitimate interests;
    portability — receive your data in a common format;
    withdraw consent at any time, where processing is based on consent;
    complain to a data protection supervisory authority. In Germany, the competent authority is the one for the federal state in which the controller is established.

To exercise any of these rights, contact us at support.jma@proton.me. We will respond within one month. Note that deleting ticket data may make it impossible for us to continue handling the matter concerned.

IMPORTANT: Deletion requests cannot be submitted through Discord. They must be sent via email to support.jma@proton.me.

Regarding DeepSeek: you do not have direct rights vis-a-vis DeepSeek. You can ask us to request deletion from DeepSeek on your behalf, but we cannot guarantee DeepSeek will comply as they are an independent data processor under their own policies.

  10  AUTOMATED DECISION-MAKING

We use automated processing to check your ticket message against our FAQ and provide a suggested answer. This is not an automated decision that produces legal effects or similarly significantly affects you — it is simply a suggested answer that you can accept or ignore. Final resolution always involves human staff if you choose to continue the conversation.

   11 AGE

Discord requires users to be at least 13 years old (older in some countries). The bot is not directed at anyone below Discord's minimum age, and we do not knowingly process their data. If you believe a minor has submitted data through the bot, contact us and we will delete it.

  12  CHANGES TO THIS POLICY

We may update this policy, for example if the bot's features or the law change. The current version is always available through the bot's Privacy Policy button. We will announce material changes in our announcement channel.

